  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of lifesaving humanitarian assistance through comprehensive site management and coordination services in displacement sites in Ma&#x2019;rib and Al Hodeidah, Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To address the urgent needs of the most vulnerable populations in displacement sites across Yemen, IOM plans to provide essential Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) activities across 53 displacement sites, hosting a total of 161,370 internally displaced persons  (IDPs) or 31,207 households (HHs) in Ma&#x2019;rib (Ma&#x2019;rib City and Ma&#x2019;rib Al Wadi districts) and Al Hodeidah (Al Khukhah and At Tuhayta districts). IOM target 34 sites in Ma&#x2019;rib, with a total population of 122,096 individuals (23,210 HHs), and 19 sites in Al Hodeidah, with a total population of 39,274 individuals (7,997 HHs). This project targets a grand total of 161,370 IDPs and host communities with CCCM engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
